<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Wave-0 H7/D1 proof (issue #119, contract items 3 and 41).

    Decision D1 says the FACADE fires the engine's reactive events (Added / Changed(old,new) /
    Removed / world-singleton notifications / value-predicate membership) and Arch's own events stay
    off. This project is the runnable evidence that the design survives an archetype backend in the
    two shapes that can break it:

      * M10  — a handler that performs a STRUCTURAL mutation while the event is in flight
               (TransformCollisionDetectionSystem.cs:87-95 Sets ColliderTagComponent from inside a
               ComponentAdded handler, and discards the subscription handle at :74-75);
      * item 41 — a singleton handler that disposes and creates entities EN MASSE and publishes a
               message per creation (the LDtk parsers: LDtkTileParserSystem.cs:41-48, :50-136, :138-156).

      cd scratchpad/arch-spike/facade-events-proof && dotnet run -c Release

    Exit code == number of failed checks, so "it compiled" and "it holds" stay separate claims.

    References Arch directly and nothing from MonoDreams: this tree rides the `scratchpad/` allowlist
    entry of the wave-1 EcsBoundaryLintTests (plan D15). Console only — the WASM and NativeAOT legs
    were proved by the sibling heads, and nothing here is target-specific.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <RootNamespace>MonoDreams.ArchSpike.FacadeEventsProof</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>FacadeEventsProof</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Same pin as MonoDreams.Benchmarks and the other spike heads (wave-0 decision: Arch 2.1.0).
         No Arch.AOT.SourceGenerator here: this head is JIT-only, so component registration (and the
         namespace shim it needs against 2.1.0) is out of scope — see ../README.md finding 1. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Arch" Version="2.1.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
